<<
/A 994 0 R
/Alt (Diagram illustrating three configurations for a running motion analysis. Panel A shows a figure with a seventeen-sensor system as the gold standard. Panel B shows minimal configurations tested: B1 with lumbar-only, B2 with ankles-only, and B3 with lumbar and ankles. Panel C outlines a machine learning pipeline, starting from minimal IMU raw signals, proceeding to feature engineering, feeding into a machine learning model using random forest, and culminating in predicted gait parameters such as ground contact time, velocity, and step length.)
